update public.moo_versions set body_md = body_md || E'<th><p>Time: At deactivation and quarterly</p>\n<p>Control: Reconciled with the Accountant</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** SP declaration; FIN-F05; certifications; procurement records; IAR; stock cards; distribution summaries; FIN-F03.\n\n### SOP 6-05 \\| Anticipatory Action Funding and Disbursement Under a State of Imminent Disaster\n**Process owner:** CDRRMO Head with the City Budget Office, City Accountant, City Treasurer and BAC. **Purpose:** Release AA funds immediately and lawfully once a State of Imminent Disaster is declared, within the 10% ceiling and the tranche rule, and account for them in the 45-day report.\n\n**Table 6.18**\n\n**SOP 6-05 Control Block**\n\n| **Control Element**         | **Entry**                                                                                                                 |\n|-----------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Type and MODE template      | Protocol: PR-AA-FUNDS                                                                                                     |\n| Decision authority (legal)  | City Mayor declares the State of Imminent Disaster (SOP GOV-05); expenditure approvals within the appropriation           |\n| Process owner (operational) | CDRRMO Head; EOC Finance and Administration desk                                                                          |\n| Trigger                     | Mayor''s declaration of a State of Imminent Disaster; a revised impact forecast during the declaration                     |\n| Forms                       | FIN-F06; FIN-F07; FIN-F09 (donations); LOG-F01                                                                            |\n| IAT v1.7 indicators         | A4.6 (0, High); A10.8 (0, High); B6.6 (1, Medium)                                                                         |\n| Functional MR links         | MR-08; MR-16; MR-07                                                                                                       |\n| Policy basis                | RA 12287 Secs. 6–7; IRR Rule IV; Rule V Secs. 1–3; Rule VI Sec. 1; RA 12009 Sec. 35(b)                                    |\n| Cross-references            | SOP GOV-05 (PR-SOID-REQUEST, PR-LIFT-REPORT); Chapter 4 PDRA and AA execution; SOPs 6-07, 6-11; Chapter 7 (45-day report) |\n\n**Table 6.19**\n\n**SOP 6-05 Steps and Controls**\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and Decision Rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and Outputs / Records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, Control and Escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Confirm declaration</th>\n<th>EOC Finance and Administration desk</th>\n<th><p>Confirm the Mayor''s declaration, hazard, area, forecast impact time and hazard family.</p>\n<p>Decision: Declaration in force?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Mayor''s EO</p>\n<p>Out: FIN-F06 header; MODE declaration record</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: On declaration</p>\n<p>Control: EO attached</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Set the envelope</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head with Budget Officer</th>\n<th><p>Record the AA allocation available (LDRRMFIP line less prior use) and other sources (STF, donations, partners).</p>\n<p>Decision: Envelope known?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: LDRRMFIP; FIN-F04</p>\n<p>Out: FIN-F06 envelope</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within 1 hour</p>\n<p>Control: Figures from the books, not estimates</p>\n<p>Escalate: City Mayor</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Match measures</th>\n<th>EOC Operations with sector leads</th>\n<th><p>Match each AA measure in the PDRA to a source, amount and lead office, net of stock already on hand (LOG-F01); size it to the forecast impact.</p>\n<p>Decision: Measure in the approved PDRA?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: PDRA; stock cards</p>\n<p>Out: Measure list</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within 2 hours</p>\n<p>Control: Each measure has a lead office</p>\n<p>Escalate: EOC Manager</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Apply the tranche rule</th>\n<th>EOC Finance and Administration desk</th>\n<th><p>For hydrometeorological and geological hazards: interventions more than 3 days before impact up to 30% of the AA allocation; within 3 days, up to 70%. Other sources are not graduated.</p>\n<p>Decision: Within the cap for its timing? Over the cap: reschedule or use a non-graduated source.</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Measure list</p>\n<p>Out: FIN-F06 tranche check (MODE computes from aa_rules)</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Before each release</p>\n<p>Control: MODE tranche value recorded</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Certify and release</th>\n<th>Budget Officer; Accountant; Treasurer</th>\n<th><p>Certify and release immediately.</p>\n<p>Decision: Certified?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: FIN-F06</p>\n<p>Out: Certifications; cash or POs</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Same day</p>\n<p>Control: Obligation reference recorded in MODE</p>\n<p>Escalate: City Administrator</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Procure</th>\n<th>BAC/HoPE</th>\n<th><p>Call off framework agreements and pre-arranged suppliers; otherwise negotiated procurement – emergency cases where its ground exists (SOP 6-07).</p>\n<p>Decision: Ground recorded?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: FIN-F08</p>\n<p>Out: Contracts; POs</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Per lead time</p>\n<p>Control: FIN-F07 where used</p>\n<p>Escalate: HoPE</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>7. Deliver and record</th>\n<th>Lead offices; CGSO; CSWDO</th>\n<th><p>Deliver AA measures; keep receipts and distribution summaries. No Regrets: goods still reach intended beneficiaries if impact does not occur.</p>\n<p>Decision: Delivered as planned?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: POs; stock</p>\n<p>Out: Delivery and distribution records</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Until lifting</p>\n<p>Control: Aggregates only in the CDRRMO file</p>\n<p>Escalate: EOC Manager</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>8. Close and report</th>\n<th>Administration and Training; City Accountant</th>\n<th><p>On lifting, total AA spending by source and measure; unused AA funds accrue to the STF; feed the 45-day report.</p>\n<p>Decision: Report on time?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: FIN-F06; vouchers</p>\n<p>Out: FIN-F06 closure; PR-LIFT-REPORT input</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within 45 days of lifting (Rule VI Sec. 1)</p>\n<p>Control: Totals reconciled with the books</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head and CDRRMC if late</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Mayor''s EO; FIN-F06 (envelope, tranche checks, closure); certifications; procurement records; delivery and distribution records; 45-day report input.\n\n### SOP 6-06 \\| Pre-Arranged Supply: Supplier List, Framework Agreements and Standard Specifications\n**Process owner:** CDRRMO Administration and Training, with the CGSO and the BAC Secretariat. **Purpose:** Make emergency and AA purchases fast and lawful by agreeing suppliers, items and prices before the event.\n\n**Table 6.20**\n\n**SOP 6-06 Control Block**\n\n| **Control Element**         | **Entry**                                                                            |\n|-----------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Type and MODE template      | Workflow: WF-SOP6-06 (seeded as WF-SOP5-06)                                          |\n| Decision authority (legal)  | BAC recommends; HoPE approves framework agreements                                   |\n| Process owner (operational) | CDRRMO Administration and Training                                                   |\n| Trigger                     | Annually before the typhoon season; after an event that exposed a supply gap         |\n| Forms                       | FIN-F08; LOG-F03 (commitment entry)                                                  |\n| IAT v1.7 indicators         | A4.5 (2, Medium); B6.6 (1, Medium); B6.3 (2, Medium)                                 |\n| Functional MR links         | MR-08; MR-16; MR-18                                                                  |\n| Policy basis                | RA 12009 Secs. 16 and 35(b) and IRR; GPPB Circular No. 07-2026; RA 12287 IRR Rule IV |\n| Cross-references            | SOPs 6-05, 6-07, 6-11, 6-12                                                          |\n\n**Table 6.21**\n\n**SOP 6-06 Steps and Controls**\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and Decision Rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and Outputs / Records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, Control and Escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. List needs</th>\n<th>Administration and Training with EOC Logistics and CSWDO</th>\n<th><p>List recurrent emergency and AA items from contingency plans, stock plans (Annex 6-D) and past events.</p>\n<p>Decision: Each item traced to a plan or AAR?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: CPs; AARs; Annex 6-D</p>\n<p>Out: Item list</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: By March</p>\n<p>Control: Source of each item stated</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Specify</th>\n<th>Administration and Training with CGSO</th>\n<th><p>Write standard specifications and price references.</p>\n<p>Decision: Specification complete?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Item list</p>\n<p>Out: Specification sheets</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: By April</p>\n<p>Control: CGSO review</p>\n<p>Escalate: CGSO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Choose the mode</th>\n<th>BAC Secretariat</th>\n<th><p>Advise on framework agreement or other mode per item.</p>\n<p>Decision: Framework agreement suitable?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Specifications</p>\n<p>Out: Procurement strategy</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: By April</p>\n<p>Control: Per GPPB Circular No. 07-2026</p>\n<p>Escalate: BAC Chair</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Procure agreements</th>\n<th>BAC; HoPE</th>\n<th><p>Run the procurement; award framework agreements with call-off trigger, maximum quantity, price basis and delivery time.</p>\n<p>Decision: Awarded?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Strategy</p>\n<p>Out: Agreements; framework agreement list</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Before June</p>\n<p>Control: Templates of GPPB Circular No. 07-2026 used</p>\n<p>Escalate: HoPE</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Register</th>\n<th>Administration and Training</th>\n<th><p>Record each supplier and agreement on FIN-F08 and in the resource inventory (LOG-F03).</p>\n<p>Decision: Recorded in both?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Agreements</p>\n<p>Out: FIN-F08; LOG-F03</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: On award</p>\n<p>Control: One entry per agreement</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Test</th>\n<th>EOC Logistics</th>\n<th><p>Confirm contact and capacity before the season; call-down test in a drill.</p>\n<p>Decision: Supplier reachable and able to deliver? If not, replace.</p></th>\n<th><p>In: FIN-F08</p>\n<p>Out: Test record</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Each season</p>\n<p>Control: Test date on LOG-F03</p>\n<p>Escalate: BAC Secretariat</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Item list; specification sheets; procurement strategy; agreements; FIN-F08; LOG-F03; test records.\n\n### SOP 6-07 \\| Emergency Procurement (Negotiated Procurement – Emergency Cases)\n**Process owner:** EOC Finance and Administration desk with the BAC. **Purpose:** Buy what an emergency requires, quickly and with its legal ground on record.\n\n**Table 6.22**\n\n**SOP 6-07 Control Block**\n\n| **Control Element**         | **Entry**                                                                                       |\n|-----------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Type and MODE template      | Protocol: PR-EMERGENCY-PROCURE                                                                  |\n| Decision authority (legal)  | HoPE on BAC recommendation, per RA 12009 IRR                                                    |\n| Process owner (operational) | EOC Finance and Administration desk; requesting office                                          |\n| Trigger                     | An urgent need during a State of Calamity or where time is of the essence because of a calamity |\n| Forms                       | FIN-F07; EOC-F06 (resource request)                                                             |\n| IAT v1.7 indicators         | A4.5 (2, Medium)                                                                                |\n| Functional MR links         | MR-08                                                                                           |\n| Policy basis                | RA 12009 Sec. 35(b) and IRR; GPPB Circular No. 06-2026                                          |\n| Cross-references            | Chapter 4 SOP 4-07; SOPs 6-04, 6-05, 6-06                                                       |\n\n**Table 6.23**\n\n**SOP 6-07 Steps and Controls**\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and Decision Rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and Outputs / Records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, Control and Escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Check pre-arranged supply</th>\n<th>EOC Finance and Administration desk</th>\n<th><p>Use stock, framework agreements or mutual aid first.</p>\n<p>Decision: Can stock or a call-off meet the need?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: EOC-F06; LOG-F01; FIN-F08</p>\n<p>Out: Sourcing decision</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Immediately</p>\n<p>Control: Decision recorded on EOC-F06</p>\n<p>Escalate: EOC Manager</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. State the ground</th>\n<th>Requesting office</th>\n<th><p>Write the ground on FIN-F07: State of Calamity reference, or the calamity and why immediate action is needed; item, quantity and use.</p>\n<p>Decision: Does the ground exist? If not, use the normal mode.</p></th>\n<th><p>In: EOC-F06</p>\n<p>Out: FIN-F07</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Before purchase</p>\n<p>Control: Ground written before purchase</p>\n<p>Escalate: BAC Chair</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Confirm funds</th>\n<th>Budget Officer; Accountant</th>\n<th><p>Certify the charging (QRF, 70% line, AA line, STF, donation).</p>\n<p>Decision: Charging matches the open window?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: FIN-F07</p>\n<p>Out: Certifications</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Same day</p>\n<p>Control: Charging recorded</p>\n<p>Escalate: City Administrator</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Negotiate</th>\n<th>BAC, or as the IRR allows</th>\n<th><p>Negotiate with a qualified supplier; collect the documents GPPB Circular No. 06-2026 requires; limit to what the emergency requires.</p>\n<p>Decision: Supplier qualified?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: FIN-F07</p>\n<p>Out: Abstract; award recommendation</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Hours</p>\n<p>Control: Documents complete</p>\n<p>Escalate: HoPE</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Award</th>\n<th>HoPE</th>\n<th><p>Approve the award and the contract or PO.</p>\n<p>Decision: Approved?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Recommendation</p>\n<p>Out: Contract or PO</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Same day</p>\n<p>Control: Signed award</p>\n<p>Escalate: —</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Accept</th>\n<th>Inspection team; CGSO</th>\n<th><p>Inspect and accept delivery; enter stock items on the stock card.</p>\n<p>Decision: Delivery conforms?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Delivery</p>\n<p>Out: IAR; LOG-F01</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: On delivery</p>\n<p>Control: IAR signed</p>\n<p>Escalate: CGSO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>7. Post and report</th>\n<th>BAC Secretariat</th>\n<th><p>Post and report as RA 12009 IRR and GPPB rules require.</p>\n<p>Decision: Posted on time?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Award</p>\n<p>Out: Posting proof</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within the required period</p>\n<p>Control: Proof filed</p>\n<p>Escalate: BAC Chair</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** EOC-F06; FIN-F07; certifications; abstract; award; contract or PO; IAR; stock card; posting proof.\n\n### SOP 6-08 \\| Donations and External Assistance: Receipt, Recording, Custody, Use and Disclosure\n**Process owner:** CSWDO and CGSO with the City Treasurer and City Accountant; the CDRRMO coordinates through the EOC. **Purpose:** Receive donations transparently and use them as the donor and the law intend.\n\n**Table 6.24**\n\n**SOP 6-08 Control Block**\n\n| **Control Element**         | **Entry**                                                                             |\n|-----------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Type and MODE template      | Workflow: WF-SOP6-08 (seeded as WF-SOP5-08)                                           |\n| Decision authority (legal)  | City Mayor accepts per SP Res. No. 2024-102                                           |\n| Process owner (operational) | CSWDO (relief goods); CGSO (property); Treasurer (cash)                               |\n| Trigger                     | An offer or delivery of cash or in-kind assistance                                    |\n| Forms                       | FIN-F09; LOG-F01                                                                      |\n| IAT v1.7 indicators         | B6.4 (2, Low)                                                                         |\n| Functional MR links         | MR-08                                                                                 |\n| Policy basis                | SP Res. No. 2024-102; COA Circular No. 2012-002; RA 12287 IRR Rule V Sec. 2; RA 10173 |\n| Cross-references            | SOP 6-11; Chapter 8 (partners)                                                        |\n\n**Table 6.25**\n\n**SOP 6-08 Steps and Controls**\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and Decision Rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and Outputs / Records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, Control and Escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Receive offer</th>\n<th>Intake desk (CSWDO/CGSO)</th>\n<th><p>Record donor type, offer, conditions and value.</p>\n<p>Decision: Suitable and acceptable? Unsuitable goods are declined at intake.</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Offer</p>\n<p>Out: FIN-F09 (draft)</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: On offer</p>\n<p>Control: Conditions recorded</p>\n<p>Escalate: CSWDO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Accept</th>\n<th>City Mayor or delegate</th>\n<th><p>Accept per SP Res. No. 2024-102; issue deed of acceptance or acknowledgement.</p>\n<p>Decision: Accepted?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: FIN-F09</p>\n<p>Out: Acceptance document</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Same day where possible</p>\n<p>Control: Signed acceptance</p>\n<p>Escalate: City Mayor</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Take custody</th>\n<th>Treasurer (cash); CGSO/CSWDO (goods)</th>\n<th><p>Deposit cash; inspect, value and store goods; enter goods on the stock card.</p>\n<p>Decision: Received as offered?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Acceptance</p>\n<p>Out: Official receipt; LOG-F01</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: On receipt</p>\n<p>Control: Receipt matches acceptance</p>\n<p>Escalate: CGSO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Record</th>\n<th>City Accountant</th>\n<th><p>Book as a receipt from other sources, kept to its purpose.</p>\n<p>Decision: Purpose recorded?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: OR; FIN-F09</p>\n<p>Out: Accounting entry</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within the month</p>\n<p>Control: Entry references FIN-F09</p>\n<p>Escalate: City Accountant</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Use</th>\n<th>Lead office</th>\n<th><p>Use per donor conditions; record distribution in aggregates.</p>\n<p>Decision: Within donor conditions?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Stock</p>\n<p>Out: Issue slips; summaries</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Per plan</p>\n<p>Control: Aggregates only</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Report and disclose</th>\n<th>Administration and Training</th>\n<th><p>Report receipts, use and balances in FIN-F03 and to donors; disclose.</p>\n<p>Decision: Disclosed?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Records</p>\n<p>Out: Report; posting</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Quarterly and at event close</p>\n<p>Control: Posting proof</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** FIN-F09; acceptance; official receipts; stock cards; accounting entries; distribution summaries; reports and postings.\n\n### SOP 6-09 \\| Fund Adequacy Test and Risk Financing, Including Insurance of Public Assets\n**Process owner:** CDRRMO Research and Planning with the City Budget Office, CGSO and CPDO. **Purpose:** Know how far City funds and stocks cover a severe credible event and close the gap with insurance and pre-arranged sources.\n\n**Table 6.26**\n\n**SOP 6-09 Control Block**\n\n| **Control Element**         | **Entry**                                                                          |\n|-----------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Type and MODE template      | Workflow: WF-SOP6-09 (seeded as WF-SOP5-09)                                        |\n| Decision authority (legal)  | CDRRMC recommends; SP appropriates premiums and contingent measures                |\n| Process owner (operational) | CDRRMO Research and Planning                                                       |\n| Trigger                     | Annually before the LDRRMFIP; after a major event or a CDRA update                 |\n| Forms                       | FIN-F10                                                                            |\n| IAT v1.7 indicators         | A4.9 (1, Medium); A4.7 (3, Low); A9.5 (1, Medium)                                  |\n| Functional MR links         | MR-08; MR-18; MR-11                                                                |\n| Policy basis                | RA 10121 Sec. 21; RA 656; RA 10174 (PSF); UNDRR Scorecard Essential 3; NEDA (2020) |\n| Cross-references            | SOP 6-01; Chapter 5 SOP 5-01 (recovery financing map)                              |\n\n**Table 6.27**\n\n**SOP 6-09 Steps and Controls**\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and Decision Rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and Outputs / Records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, Control and Escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Choose scenarios</th>\n<th>Research and Planning</th>\n<th><p>Use the most severe credible scenarios of the flood and tropical cyclone contingency plans (for example, a Thelma-type flash flood; a Yolanda-strength typhoon).</p>\n<p>Decision: Same scenarios as Chapter 3?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: CPs; CDRA</p>\n<p>Out: Scenario sheet</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: With the budget call</p>\n<p>Control: Assumptions stated</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Cost the response</th>\n<th>Research and Planning with CSWDO, City Engineer, CHO</th>\n<th><p>Cost relief, evacuation, debris clearing, emergency repair and early recovery from the plans.</p>\n<p>Decision: Every cost sourced?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Scenario sheet</p>\n<p>Out: Cost estimate</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Two weeks</p>\n<p>Control: Unit costs dated</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Compare</th>\n<th>Research and Planning with Budget Office</th>\n<th><p>Compare with stock on hand, QRF, AA line, STF, insurance cover and other sources.</p>\n<p>Decision: Shortfall?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Cost estimate; ledgers; LOG-F01</p>\n<p>Out: FIN-F10 shortfall</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: —</p>\n<p>Control: Figures from the books</p>\n<p>Escalate: City Budget Officer</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Check insurance</th>\n<th>CGSO</th>\n<th><p>Confirm the EOC, evacuation centres, warehouses and critical facilities on the GSIS indemnity schedule; list uninsured priority assets.</p>\n<p>Decision: Priority assets insured?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: GSIS schedule</p>\n<p>Out: Insurance schedule</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Before renewal</p>\n<p>Control: Schedule current</p>\n<p>Escalate: CGSO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Recommend</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head</th>\n<th><p>Propose premiums, STF reserves, stock levels, framework agreements, PSF proposals and fallback sources.</p>\n<p>Decision: Recommendations costed?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: FIN-F10</p>\n<p>Out: Recommendations into SOP 6-01</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Before the LDRRMFIP draft</p>\n<p>Control: CDRRMC notes the test</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMC</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Scenario sheet; cost estimate; FIN-F10; insurance schedule; recommendations.\n\n### SOP 6-10 \\| Audit Readiness, COA Observations and Internal Control\n**Process owner:** CDRRMO Administration and Training, with the City Accountant and the Internal Audit Service, where constituted. **Purpose:** Prevent common findings and close COA observations on DRRM funds, stocks and property.\n\n**Table 6.28**\n\n**SOP 6-10 Control Block**\n\n| **Control Element**         | **Entry**                                                                                                            |\n|-----------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Type and MODE template      | Workflow: WF-SOP6-10 (seeded as WF-SOP5-10)                                                                          |\n| Decision authority (legal)  | City Mayor answers COA; COA decides                                                                                  |\n| Process owner (operational) | CDRRMO Administration and Training                                                                                   |\n| Trigger                     | Before year-end (pre-audit check); receipt of an Audit Observation Memorandum (AOM) or the Annual Audit Report (AAR) |\n| Forms                       | FIN-F11                                                                                                              |\n| IAT v1.7 indicators         | A4.8 (2, Medium)                                                                                                     |\n| Functional MR links         | MR-08; MR-11; MR-14                                                                                                  |\n| Policy basis                | COA Circular No. 2012-002; COA rules on AOMs and AARs; COA property rules                                            |\n| Cross-references            | Annex 6-B; Chapter 7 (corrective action register)                                                                    |\n\n**Table 6.29**\n\n**SOP 6-10 Steps and Controls**\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and Decision Rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and Outputs / Records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, Control and Escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Pre-audit check</th>\n<th>Administration and Training with Accountant</th>\n<th><p>Run the Annex 6-B checklist on the year''s DRRM transactions.</p>\n<p>Decision: Any "No"? Each becomes a corrective action on FIN-F11.</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Transactions</p>\n<p>Out: Checklist record</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: By November</p>\n<p>Control: Checklist signed</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Physical count</th>\n<th>CGSO with CDRRMO</th>\n<th><p>Count DRRM property and stocks and reconcile with the asset register and stock cards.</p>\n<p>Decision: Variance?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Registers; stock cards</p>\n<p>Out: Count report</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Per COA schedule</p>\n<p>Control: Variances explained</p>\n<p>Escalate: CGSO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Log observations</th>\n<th>Administration and Training</th>\n<th><p>Log each AOM or AAR finding on DRRM funds, stocks or property.</p>\n<p>Decision: Logged?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: AOM; AAR</p>\n<p>Out: FIN-F11</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: On receipt</p>\n<p>Control: Copied to the Chapter 7 register</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Respond</th>\n<th>Responsible office</th>\n<th><p>Prepare the reply and corrective action with evidence.</p>\n<p>Decision: Evidence attached?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: FIN-F11</p>\n<p>Out: Reply; action plan</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within the period COA sets</p>\n<p>Control: Reply reviewed by the City Accountant</p>\n<p>Escalate: City Mayor</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Track</th>\n<th>Administration and Training</th>\n<th><p>Report open findings to the CDRRMC each quarter.</p>\n<p>Decision: Overdue?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: FIN-F11</p>\n<p>Out: FIN-F03 annex</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Quarterly</p>\n<p>Control: Status dated</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Close</th>\n<th>COA (external); City Accountant</th>\n<th><p>Record COA''s status of implementation.</p>\n<p>Decision: Implemented?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Next AAR</p>\n<p>Out: FIN-F11 closed</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Next AAR</p>\n<p>Control: Closure only on COA status</p>\n<p>Escalate: —</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Annex 6-B checklist; count report; FIN-F11; replies; quarterly status; COA status of implementation.\n\n### SOP 6-11 \\| Prepositioned Relief Stocks: Levels, Warehousing, Rotation and Replenishment\n**Process owner:** CSWDO (custody of relief goods) and CGSO (warehousing and property), with CDRRMO Administration and Training. **Purpose:** Keep relief stocks at levels set from the contingency plan scenarios, safe, rotated before expiry and replenished in time.\n\n**Table 6.30**\n\n**SOP 6-11 Control Block**\n\n| **Control Element**         | **Entry**                                                                                                                                                              |\n|-----------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Type and MODE template      | Workflow: WF-SOP6-11 (proposed)                                                                                                                                        |\n| Decision authority (legal)  | CDRRMO Head approves the stock plan with the CSWDO Head; funding through SOP 6-01; issue under the authority of the CSWDO and the EOC request route                    |\n| Process owner (operational) | CSWDO; CGSO; CDRRMO Administration and Training                                                                                                                        |\n| Trigger                     | Annual stock plan before the typhoon season; stock at the reorder point; item within its rotation window; receipt of goods; an alert level or forecast under Chapter 4 |\n| Forms                       | LOG-F01; LOG-F02; Annex 6-D                                                                                                                                            |\n| IAT v1.7 indicators         | A7.5 (3, Low); A4.9 (1, Medium)                                                                                                                                        |\n| Functional MR links         | MR-04; MR-08                                                                                                                                                           |\n| Policy basis                | RA 10121; NDRRMC Disaster Preparedness Minimum Standards Vol. 2; COA property rules; RA 10173                                                                          |\n| Cross-references            | Chapter 3 SOP 3-06; Chapter 4 section 7.3 and SOP 4-07; SOPs 6-04, 6-05, 6-06                                                                                          |\n\n**Table 6.31**\n\n**SOP 6-11 Steps and Controls**\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and Decision Rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and Outputs / Records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, Control and Escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Set levels</th>\n<th>CSWDO with CDRRMO Research and Planning</th>\n<th><p>Compute target levels and reorder points by item and warehouse from the scenarios (Annex 6-D); not below the DPMS minimum.</p>\n<p>Decision: Levels traced to a scenario?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: CPs; DPMS Vol. 2</p>\n<p>Out: Annex 6-D stock plan</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: By March</p>\n<p>Control: Approved by the CDRRMO Head and CSWDO Head</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMC if unfunded</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Check warehouses</th>\n<th>CGSO with CDRRMO</th>\n<th><p>Inspect each warehouse for hazard exposure, condition, security and access.</p>\n<p>Decision: Fit for use? If not, move stock and record the decision.</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Hazard maps; site</p>\n<p>Out: LOG-F02 inspection</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Before the typhoon season and quarterly</p>\n<p>Control: Inspection signed</p>\n<p>Escalate: CGSO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Receive</th>\n<th>Custodian (CSWDO or CGSO)</th>\n<th><p>Inspect and accept; enter quantity, batch and expiry on the stock card and in MODE.</p>\n<p>Decision: Matches the IAR?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Deliveries; IAR</p>\n<p>Out: LOG-F01; MODE resource record</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: On receipt</p>\n<p>Control: One item, one record</p>\n<p>Escalate: CGSO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Rotate</th>\n<th>Custodian</th>\n<th><p>Issue items within their rotation window to regular programmes or drills, first expiry first out.</p>\n<p>Decision: Item within its rotation window?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: LOG-F01</p>\n<p>Out: Issue slips</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Monthly review</p>\n<p>Control: No expired stock on hand</p>\n<p>Escalate: CSWDO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Replenish</th>\n<th>Custodian; Administration and Training</th>\n<th><p>When an item reaches its reorder point, raise replenishment against the open window: stock line, AA line or QRF.</p>\n<p>Decision: Which window is open?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: LOG-F01</p>\n<p>Out: Replenishment request; call-off</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Same week; same day under an alert</p>\n<p>Control: Charging cites the window</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Issue in events</th>\n<th>Custodian on EOC request (SOP 4-07)</th>\n<th><p>Issue against an approved request; record aggregates; update the stock card and MODE.</p>\n<p>Decision: Request approved?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: EOC-F06</p>\n<p>Out: Issue slips; distribution summary</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Per request</p>\n<p>Control: Named lists stay with the CSWDO</p>\n<p>Escalate: EOC Manager</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>7. Count and report</th>\n<th>Custodian with CGSO</th>\n<th><p>Monthly spot count; annual physical count; report levels against targets in FIN-F03.</p>\n<p>Decision: Variance?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: LOG-F01</p>\n<p>Out: Count report; FIN-F03 entry</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Monthly; annually</p>\n<p>Control: Variances explained in writing</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Annex 6-D stock plan; LOG-F02 inspections; IARs; LOG-F01 stock cards; MODE resource records; issue slips; count reports.\n\n### SOP 6-12 \\| DRRM Resource Inventory and Pre-Arranged Commitments\n**Process owner:** CDRRMO Administration and Training (inventory custodian), with the CGSO, BDRRMCs and partners. **Purpose:** Give the EOC one current view of City, barangay, partner and supplier resources and the commitments behind them.\n\n**Table 6.32**\n\n**SOP 6-12 Control Block**\n\n| **Control Element**         | **Entry**                                                                                                              |\n|-----------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Type and MODE template      | Workflow: WF-SOP6-12 (proposed)                                                                                        |\n| Decision authority (legal)  | Each owner decides on release of its own resources; agreements signed by the competent authority (Chapter 8)           |\n| Process owner (operational) | CDRRMO Administration and Training                                                                                     |\n| Trigger                     | Annual update before the typhoon season; new agreement or equipment; result of a call-down test; after each activation |\n| Forms                       | LOG-F03                                                                                                                |\n| IAT v1.7 indicators         | B6.3 (2, Medium); B6.6 (1, Medium); A8.3 (3, Low); A10.1 (1, Medium)                                                   |\n| Functional MR links         | MR-08; MR-05                                                                                                           |\n| Policy basis                | RA 10121; ICS resource management (NDRRMC MC No. 4, s. 2012); RA 12287 IRR Rule IV                                     |\n| Cross-references            | Chapter 4 SOP 4-07; SOP 6-06; Chapter 8 (agreements)                                                                   |\n\n**Table 6.33**\n\n**SOP 6-12 Steps and Controls**\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and Decision Rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and Outputs / Records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, Control and Escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Copy City assets</th>\n<th>Inventory custodian with CGSO</th>\n<th><p>Copy City-owned DRRM equipment and vehicles from the property records, with serviceability and maintenance date.</p>\n<p>Decision: Matches the asset register?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: PAR/ICS; maintenance log</p>\n<p>Out: LOG-F03 entries; MODE resources</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: By April</p>\n<p>Control: One item, one record</p>\n<p>Escalate: CGSO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Collect barangay data</th>\n<th>Inventory custodian with BDRRMCs</th>\n<th><p>Collect BDRRMC equipment and stocks by template.</p>\n<p>Decision: All 85 barangays reported? Blank means "not reported", not zero.</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Barangay templates</p>\n<p>Out: LOG-F03 entries</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: By April</p>\n<p>Control: Reporting rate recorded</p>\n<p>Escalate: DILG City Director</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Record commitments</th>\n<th>Inventory custodian</th>\n<th><p>Record partner and supplier resources only with the agreement, item, quantity, activation trigger and contact position.</p>\n<p>Decision: Signed commitment exists? If not, list as "potential", not available.</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Agreements; FIN-F08</p>\n<p>Out: LOG-F03 commitment entries</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: On signing</p>\n<p>Control: Agreement reference attached</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Confirm</th>\n<th>EOC Logistics</th>\n<th><p>Confirm availability by call-down; mark entries not confirmed in 12 months as unconfirmed.</p>\n<p>Decision: Confirmed?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: LOG-F03</p>\n<p>Out: Confirmation dates</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Before the season</p>\n<p>Control: Test record</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Publish to the EOC</th>\n<th>Inventory custodian</th>\n<th><p>Make the inventory available to the EOC in MODE and in a printed copy for the alternate EOC.</p>\n<p>Decision: Current printed copy at both sites?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: LOG-F03</p>\n<p>Out: EOC inventory view; printout</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: After each update</p>\n<p>Control: Print date on the copy</p>\n<p>Escalate: EOC Manager</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>6. Review after events</th>\n<th>Inventory custodian with EOC Logistics</th>\n<th><p>Update quantities and serviceability after demobilisation; send gaps to the Chapter 7 AAR.</p>\n<p>Decision: Gaps found?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Resource request records</p>\n<p>Out: Updated LOG-F03; AAR input</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within 30 days of deactivation</p>\n<p>Control: Changes dated</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** LOG-F03 inventory and commitment entries; agreements; confirmation records; EOC inventory view and printout; post-event updates.\n\n## 17. Responsibility Assignment (RACI)\n\n| **\\[R\\] Responsible** | **\\[A\\] Accountable** | **\\[C\\] Consulted** | **\\[I\\] Informed** |\n|-----------------------|-----------------------|---------------------|--------------------|\n\n"A" is the single proposed process-accountable owner; "R" performs; "C" is consulted; "I" is informed. The RACI allocates work; it does not transfer the legal powers named in section 3.\n\n**Table 6.34**\n\n*RACI for DRRM Financing and Resource Management*\n\n| **Activity**                    | **MY** | **SP** | **CC** | **HD** | **RP** | **AT** | **BU** | **AC** | **TR** | **BA** | **GS** | **SW** |\n|---------------------------------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|\n| LDRRMF computation              | I      | I      | I      | C      | C      | I      | A/R    | C      | C      | –      | –      | –      |\n| LDRRMFIP drafting               | I      | I      | C      | A      | R      | R      | C      | C      | –      | C      | C      | C      |\n| LDRRMFIP approval / adoption    | I      | A      | A      | R      | R      | I      | C      | C      | –      | –      | –      | –      |\n| Utilisation tracking and report | I      | I      | I      | A      | R      | R      | C      | R      | C      | I      | I      | I      |\n| STF ageing and programming      | I      | A      | A      | C      | R      | I      | C      | R      | C      | –      | –      | –      |\n| QRF use                         | A      | A      | C      | R      | C      | R      | R      | R      | R      | R      | R      | R      |\n| AA fund release                 | A      | I      | C      | R      | C      | R      | R      | R      | R      | R      | R      | R      |\n| Pre-arranged supply             | A      | –      | I      | C      | I      | R      | C      | –      | –      | R      | R      | C      |\n| Emergency procurement           | A      | I      | I      | C      | –      | R      | R      | R      | R      | R      | R      | C      |\n| Donations                       | A      | I      | I      | C      | –      | R      | –      | R      | R      | –      | R      | R      |\n| Adequacy test and insurance     | I      | A      | C      | A      | R      | C      | C      | –      | –      | –      | R      | –      |\n| Audit response                  | A      | I      | I      | R      | C      | R      | –      | R      | C      | C      | R      | C      |\n| Prepositioned stocks            | I      | –      | I      | A      | C      | R      | C      | I      | –      | C      | R      | A      |\n| Resource inventory              | I      | –      | I      | A      | C      | R      | –      | –      | –      | –      | R      | C      |\n\n*Note. MY = City Mayor (HoPE for awards); SP = Sangguniang Panlungsod; CC = CDRRMC; HD = CDRRMO Head; RP = CDRRMO Research and Planning Division; AT = CDRRMO Administration and Training Division; BU = City Budget Office; AC = City Accountant; TR = City Treasurer; BA = BAC; GS = CGSO; SW = CSWDO. Where a row has two "A" entries, each holds a distinct legal act: the CDRRMC approves and the SP adopts or concurs (LDRRMFIP, STF); the SP declares a State of Calamity and the Mayor approves QRF spending; the Mayor declares a State of Imminent Disaster and approves AA spending; the CDRRMO Head approves the stock plan and the CSWDO holds custody of relief goods; the CDRRMO Head runs the adequacy test and the SP appropriates premiums.*\n\n## 18. Performance Monitoring, Quality Assurance and Corrective Action\n\n**Table 6.35**\n\n*Performance Measures for Chapter 6*\n\n| **Measure**                                                | **Evidence**                                                                                   | **Review Owner**             |\n|------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------|\n| LDRRMF base computed on regular revenue                    | FIN-F01 signed by the Budget Officer                                                           | CDRRMO Head; CDRRMC          |\n| LDRRMFIP lines traced to LDRRMP and CDP PPAs               | FIN-F02; share of lines with codes                                                             | Research and Planning        |\n| AA line present and within 10% of the 70%                  | LDRRMFIP; FIN-F01; MODE aa_fund_years                                                          | CDRRMC                       |\n| Utilisation of the 70% component                           | FIN-F03; target at least 80% (A4.4)                                                            | CDRRMC, quarterly            |\n| STF balances near deadline                                 | FIN-F04 flags; zero reversions                                                                 | City Accountant; CDRRMO Head |\n| QRF used only under a State of Calamity                    | FIN-F05 references                                                                             | Internal audit; COA          |\n| AA releases within the tranche rule; 45-day report on time | FIN-F06 checks; PR-LIFT-REPORT                                                                 | CDRRMO Head; OCD VIII        |\n| Emergency procurement grounds recorded before purchase     | FIN-F07                                                                                        | BAC Secretariat              |\n| Stocks at or above target; no expired stock                | LOG-F01; count reports                                                                         | CSWDO Head; CDRRMO Head      |\n| Inventory coverage and currency                            | LOG-F03: share of the 85 barangays reporting; share of entries confirmed in the last 12 months | CDRRMO Head                  |\n| Donations recorded and disclosed                           | FIN-F09; postings                                                                              | Administration and Training  |\n| COA findings closed                                        | FIN-F11 status                                                                                 | City Accountant; CDRRMO Head |\n\nCorrective actions record the finding, evidence, cause, action, accountable office, due date and verification, and go into the corrective and preventive action register run under Chapter 7 (Chapter 1, section 9.5).\n\n**Legal readings to confirm with the City Legal Office and OCD VIII before adoption:**\n\n1.  Whether the AA line may be created in the current year by realignment within the 70% component, or only in a new LDRRMFIP.\n\n2.  Whether "allocation for anticipatory action" in Rule V Sec. 2 means the year''s AA line or the amount released for one declaration.\n\n3.  The treatment of slow-onset hazards until the NDRRMC operational guidelines are issued (ADR-025 item 4).\n\n4.  Whether "time is of the essence" under RA 12009 Sec. 35(b) covers AA purchases under a State of Imminent Disaster when no State of Calamity is in force.\n\n5.  The exact composition of "estimated revenue from regular sources" for the City (A4.1).\n\n6.  Whether stock replenishment bought from the AA line for an imminent threat, and not used because the hazard did not occur, is carried as AA-funded stock or transferred to the regular stock line.\n\n## 19. Implementation, Validation and Institutionalisation Priorities\n\n**Table 6.36**\n\n*Implementation Priorities for Chapter 6*\n\n| **No.** | **Action**                                                                                                                                                                                      | **Office**                           | **IAT**      | **When**                                                                |\n|---------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------|--------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Create the AA line (up to 10% of the 70%) and write the Budget, Accounting, Treasury and BAC release steps (SOP 6-05).                                                                          | CDRRMO Head; Budget; Accounting; BAC | A4.6         | Before the next typhoon season; CDRRMC decides the route (section 10.3) |\n| 2       | Confirm the LDRRMF base and correct the year references in Res. No. 05, s. 2025.                                                                                                                | Budget Office                        | A4.1, A3.5   | Before the workshop                                                     |\n| 3       | Start quarterly utilisation reports and FDP posting.                                                                                                                                            | Administration and Training          | A4.4, A10.5  | Next CDRRMC quarterly meeting                                           |\n| 4       | Build the STF ageing ledger.                                                                                                                                                                    | City Accountant                      | A4.3         | January 2027                                                            |\n| 5       | Supplier list and framework agreements for relief goods, fuel and heavy equipment, using GPPB Circular No. 07-2026 templates.                                                                   | Administration and Training; BAC     | A4.5, B6.6   | Before June 2027                                                        |\n| 6       | Approve the first stock plan (Annex 6-D) and attach the warehouse inventory with reorder points for validation.                                                                                 | CSWDO; CDRRMO                        | A7.5         | Before the workshop for the inventory; March 2027 for the plan          |\n| 7       | Extend the resource inventory to barangays, partners and suppliers (LOG-F03).                                                                                                                   | Administration and Training          | B6.3         | April 2027                                                              |\n| 8       | Attach the latest COA Annual Audit Report and the status of DRRM findings.                                                                                                                      | Administration and Training          | A4.8         | Before the workshop                                                     |\n| 9       | Run the adequacy test for two scenarios.                                                                                                                                                        | Research and Planning                | A4.9         | With the FY 2028 budget call                                            |\n| 10      | Check GSIS coverage of the EOC, evacuation centres, warehouses and critical facilities.                                                                                                         | CGSO                                 | A4.7         | Before renewal                                                          |\n| 11      | Adopt the donations SOP by executive order and test it in a drill.                                                                                                                              | CSWDO; CGSO                          | B6.4         | Next drill                                                              |\n| 12      | Platform: re-seed Chapter 6 codes (WF-SOP5-xx to WF-SOP6-xx, with aliases); add holder type, commitment reference, reorder point and expiry to resources; add templates for SOPs 6-11 and 6-12. | Platform data custodian              | MR-08, MR-14 | With the Chapter 6 re-seed (Coherence Analysis Part III.0)              |\n\nValidation: each SOP is reviewed by the offices that hold its legal functions, tested in a tabletop exercise with the Budget, Accounting, Treasury, BAC, CGSO and CSWDO offices, and adopted only after the City Legal Office confirms the readings in section 18.\n\n## 20. Forms, Registers and Annexes\n\n**Table 6.37**\n\n*Chapter 6 Forms*\n\n| **Code** | **Form**                                                                  | **Used in**           | **MODE**                            |\n|----------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------|-------------------------------------|\n| FIN-F01  | LDRRMF computation and allocation sheet                                   | SOP 6-01              | Seeded                              |\n| FIN-F02  | LDRRMFIP thematic split                                                   | SOP 6-01              | Carried by BUD-F01                  |\n| FIN-F03  | Quarterly utilisation, stock and results report                           | SOP 6-02              | Carried by BUD-F02                  |\n| FIN-F04  | Special Trust Fund ageing ledger entry                                    | SOP 6-03              | Seeded                              |\n| FIN-F05  | QRF use request and certification                                         | SOP 6-04              | Seeded                              |\n| FIN-F06  | Anticipatory action fund release and tranche record                       | SOP 6-05              | Seeded; aa_disbursements            |\n| FIN-F07  | Emergency procurement justification and record                            | SOP 6-07              | Seeded                              |\n| FIN-F08  | Pre-arranged supplier and framework agreement register entry              | SOP 6-06              | Seeded                              |\n| FIN-F09  | Donation receipt and acknowledgement                                      | SOP 6-08              | Seeded                              |\n| FIN-F10  | Fund adequacy test                                                        | SOP 6-09              | Seeded                              |\n| FIN-F11  | Audit observation and corrective action tracker                           | SOP 6-10              | Seeded                              |\n| LOG-F01  | Stock card: item, batch, expiry, receipts, issues, balance, reorder point | SOPs 6-04, 6-05, 6-11 | Proposed; resources table extension |\n| LOG-F02  | Warehouse inspection checklist                                            | SOP 6-11              | Proposed                            |\n| LOG-F03  | Resource inventory and commitment entry                                   | SOPs 6-06, 6-12       | Proposed; resources table extension |\n\nAnnexes: **6-A** IAT and master requirements traceability; **6-B** pre-audit checklist for DRRM transactions; **6-C** anticipatory action funding pathway and tranche worksheet; **6-D** prepositioned stock planning worksheet.\n\n## 21. Relationship With Other Chapters\n\n**Table 6.38**\n\n*Links Between Chapter 6 and the Other Chapters*\n\n| **Ch.** | **Title**                                                                 | **Link**                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n|---------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Legal Mandate, DRRM Governance and Institutional Accountability           | Declares the State of Calamity (GOV-04) and the State of Imminent Disaster (GOV-05) that open the QRF and AA funds; the CDRRMC approves plans; the CAPA register is defined in section 9.5. |\n| 2       | CDRRMO Organisational Structure, Staffing and HR Management               | Staffs the Administration and Research and Planning roles that run this chapter; holds the EOC facility and continuity assets (section 2.8).                                                |\n| 3       | Risk Intelligence, Planning and Institutional Preparedness                | Sets the LDRRMP that the LDRRMFIP funds and the contingency plan scenarios that set stock levels and the adequacy test.                                                                     |\n| 4       | Early Warning, EOC Activation, Incident Management and Emergency Response | Raises resource requests (SOP 4-07, EOC-F06) and coordinates prepositioning (section 7.3); expenditure, procurement and stock issue follow this chapter.                                    |\n| 5       | Recovery, Rehabilitation and Build Back Better                            | Uses this chapter''s rules for recovery funds and procurement; its financing map (SOP 5-01) draws on the adequacy test.                                                                      |\n| 7       | Monitoring, Evaluation, Knowledge Management and Continuous Improvement   | Receives utilisation reports, COA findings and stock and inventory gaps into the reporting calendar and the CAPA register.                                                                  |\n| 8       | Stakeholder Engagement and Institutional Partnerships                     | Negotiates the mutual aid and partner agreements whose commitments this chapter records.                                                                                                    |\n| 9       | Public Awareness, Community Resilience and Capacity Development           | Trains custodians and barangays on stock and inventory procedures; drills use rotated stock.                                                                                                |\n| 10      | Institutional Sustainability, Deep Resilience and Recognition             | Uses the funding and audit record as evidence for Gawad KALASAG and SGLG.                                                                                                                   |\n\n## 22. Concluding Notes\n\nThe City already sets aside and approves its DRRM fund, and it has bought relief goods quickly when a State of Calamity allowed. The work now is to make funds and supplies reachable at the right moment and to prove what they did: an anticipatory action line before impact, a QRF under its proper trigger after impact, suppliers agreed and stocks set before the season, an inventory the EOC can trust, and records that tell the CDRRMC, the public and COA what each peso and each item did.\n\nWriting these procedures does not implement them. Until the AA line exists, the first stock plan is approved, the inventory reaches the barangays and suppliers, and at least one exercise has tested SOPs 6-04, 6-05 and 6-11 with the Budget, Accounting, Treasury, BAC, CGSO and CSWDO offices, this chapter remains a controlled working draft.\n\n## References\n\nThe official text governs.\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2023). *Ormoc City disaster risk reduction and management ten-year plan (2023–2032)*.\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2026a). *Ormoc CDRRMO–EOC institutional assessment tool* (Version 1.7) \\[Unpublished assessment workbook\\].\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2026b). *Ormoc CDRRMO–EOC master requirements traceability and 140-indicator data dictionary* (Version 1.2) \\[Unpublished project reference workbook\\].\n\nCity Government of Ormoc. (2026c). *MODE platform coherence analysis, Pareto priority indicators and final 10-chapter structure* \\[Unpublished project document\\].\n\nCity Government of Ormoc, City Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2025). *Resolution Nos. 01 to 08, series of 2025*.\n\nCity Government of Ormoc, Sangguniang Panlungsod. (2024). *Resolution Nos. 2024-088 and 2024-102*.\n\nCommission on Audit. (2012). *COA Circular No. 2012-002: Accounting and reporting guidelines for the LDRRMF, NDRRMF given to LGUs and receipts from other sources*.\n\nDepartment of the Interior and Local Government. (2012). *Memorandum Circular No. 2012-141: Full Disclosure Policy* and later issuances.\n\nGovernment Procurement Policy Board. (2026a). *Circular No. 06-2026: Documentary requirements and relevant guidelines for specific modes of procurement under RA No. 12009* (Resolution No. 10-2026, 3 February 2026).\n\nGovernment Procurement Policy Board. (2026b). *Circular No. 07-2026: Guidelines on the use of framework agreement under RA No. 12009 and its IRR* (Resolution No. 12-2026, 23 July 2026).\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2017). *Memorandum No. 147, s. 2017*.\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (n.d.). *Disaster preparedness minimum standards* (Vol. 2).\n\nNational Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Council. (2026). *Implementing rules and regulations of Republic Act No. 12287* (signed 14 September 2026).\n\nNational Economic and Development Authority. (2020). *Disaster rehabilitation and recovery planning guide*. (NEDA is now the Department of Economy, Planning, and Development under RA 12145.)\n\nNDRRMC, Department of Budget and Management, & Department of the Interior and Local Government. (2013). *Joint Memorandum Circular No. 2013-1: Allocation and utilisation of the LDRRMF*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 656. (1951). *Property Insurance Law*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 9729. (2009). *Climate Change Act of 2009*, as amended by Republic Act No. 10174 (2012).\n\nRepublic Act No. 10121. (2010). *Philippine Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Act of 2010*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 10173. (2012). *Data Privacy Act of 2012*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 12009. (2024). *New Government Procurement Act*.\n\nRepublic Act No. 12287. (2025). *Declaration of State of Imminent Disaster Act*.\n\nUnited Nations Office for Disaster Risk Reduction. (2017). *Disaster resilience scorecard for cities: Detailed level assessment*.\n\n## Annex 6-A. IAT and Master Requirements Traceability\n\n**Table 6.39**\n\n*IAT Rows, Master Requirements and Chapter 6 Procedures*\n\n| **IAT** | **Type**     | **Weight (W)** | **Score** | **Gap Priority** | **Master Requirements**              | **SOP**          | **Recommended Action (IAT v1.7)**                                                                                                              |\n|---------|--------------|----------------|-----------|------------------|--------------------------------------|------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| A3.5    | M            | 3              | 3         | 4.5 Medium       | MR-03; MR-04; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 6-01             | Tag each LDRRMFIP item to an LDRRMP and CDP PPA code;