e CDRA list.                               |\n| A4.8    | M            | 2              | 2         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15               | 6-10             | Set an internal audit check of the LDRRMF before year-end.                                                                                     |\n| A4.9    | GP           | 2              | 1         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-08; MR-18; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 6-09             | Cost response and early recovery for a Thelma-type flash flood and a Yolanda-type typhoon; record the shortfall and fallback sources.          |\n| A7.5    | M            | 2              | 3         | 3.0 Low          | MR-04; MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 6-11             | Maintain; validate the warehouse inventory and replenishment triggers; add AA prepositioning triggers.                                         |\n| A8.3    | M            | 2              | 3         | 3.0 Low          | MR-05; MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 6-12             | Programme a preventive maintenance schedule for vehicles and equipment and keep logs.                                                          |\n| A10.5   | M            | 1              | 2         | 3.0 Low          | MR-07; MR-11; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 6-02             | Maintain; attach posting proof.                                                                                                                |\n| B6.3    | M            | 2              | 2         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15               | 6-12             | Extend the inventory to barangays, partners and suppliers.                                                                                     |\n| B6.4    | GP           | 1              | 2         | 2.0 Low          | MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15               | 6-08             | Write the donations and volunteer SOP under SP Res. No. 2024-102.                                                                              |\n| B6.6    | GP           | 2              | 1         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-08; MR-16; MR-18; MR-01; MR-12–15 | 6-06, 6-12       | Sign agreements listing item, quantity, trigger and contact, usable for AA.                                                                    |\n| B7.5    | M            | 2              | 3         | 3.0 Low          | MR-04; MR-11; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 6-01             | Keep the EOC operations line in each LDRRMFIP.                                                                                                 |\n| A10.8   | M            | 2              | 0         | 12.0 High        | MR-07; MR-11; MR-16; MR-01; MR-12–15 | 6-05 step 8      | Prepare the 45-day post-declaration report template (Chapter 7) and confirm the route with OCD VIII.                                           |\n| C1.2    | CPDO; Budget | 1              | 1         | 3.0 Low          | MR-03; MR-17; MR-18; MR-01; MR-12–15 | 6-01 step 4      | Add a one-page DRR-CCA screening form to LDC/LFC project review, owned by the CPDO with CDRRMO sign-off.                                       |\n\n*Note. Copied from IAT v1.7 and the Traceability and Data Dictionary v1.2. Scores and priorities are for validation (Methodology v1.1, section 6). Part C rows carry the lead office in the Type column and are not added to the IMI.*\n\n## Annex 6-B. Pre-Audit Checklist for DRRM Transactions\n\nUsed in SOP 6-10 step 1, before year-end, by CDRRMO Administration and Training with the City Accountant. Each "No" becomes a corrective action on FIN-F11. The checklist prevents the findings COA most often raises on LDRRMF use; it does not replace COA''s own requirements.\n\n**Table 6.40**\n\n*Pre-Audit Checklist*\n\n| **No.** | **Check**                                                                                                           | **Evidence**                                                 | **Yes / No / NA** |\n|---------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| 1       | The LDRRMF was computed on estimated revenue from regular sources, and the computation is filed                     | FIN-F01 signed by the Budget Officer                         |                   |\n| 2       | The 70/30 split appears in the appropriation and in the books                                                       | Appropriation ordinance; ledgers                             |                   |\n| 3       | Every charge to the 70% is in the approved LDRRMFIP and is a DRRM use                                               | LDRRMFIP line; obligation request                            |                   |\n| 4       | Every QRF charge refers to an SP declaration of a State of Calamity in force at the time                            | SP resolution; FIN-F05                                       |                   |\n| 5       | Every AA charge refers to a State of Imminent Disaster in force, is within the AA line and passed the tranche check | Mayor''s EO; FIN-F06                                          |                   |\n| 6       | Unused QRF and 70% balances were transferred to the STF at year-end                                                 | Closing entries                                              |                   |\n| 7       | The STF ledger shows each balance by year of origin and its deadline; no balance passed five years unused           | FIN-F04                                                      |                   |\n| 8       | Each emergency procurement has its written ground, HoPE approval, documents and posting                             | FIN-F07; BAC records                                         |                   |\n| 9       | Each delivery has an inspection and acceptance report                                                               | IAR                                                          |                   |\n| 10      | Relief goods and non-food items issued have issue slips and distribution summaries                                  | Issue slips; summaries (no personal data in the CDRRMO file) |                   |\n| 11      | No stock on hand is past its expiry date; rotated items have issue records                                          | LOG-F01; count report                                        |                   |\n| 12      | Cash advances for DRRM operations were liquidated within the period                                                 | Liquidation reports                                          |                   |\n| 13      | Donations have acceptance documents, receipts and use records                                                       | FIN-F09; ORs                                                 |                   |\n| 14      | Quarterly utilisation reports were submitted to the CDRRMC and posted under the Full Disclosure Policy              | FIN-F03; posting proof                                       |                   |\n| 15      | DRRM property is on the asset register, covered by PAR or ICS, and counted this year                                | Count report                                                 |                   |\n| 16      | Insurance of DRRM buildings, warehouses and equipment is current                                                    | GSIS policy schedule                                         |                   |\n| 17      | Prior-year COA observations on DRRM funds, stocks and property have a reply and status                              | FIN-F11                                                      |                   |\n\n## Annex 6-C. Anticipatory Action Funding Pathway and Tranche Worksheet\n\nBasis: RA 12287 and its IRR (signed 14 September 2026), Rule V Secs. 1–3; ADR-025. The official text governs. DBM–COA guidelines on AA funds and NDRRMC operational guidelines are pending; this worksheet will be revised when they are issued.\n\n1.  **Plan.** The LDRRMFIP carries an AA line of no more than 10% of the 70% component, naming the AA measures (by hazard and sector), lead offices and procurement mode (SOP 6-01).\n\n2.  **Pre-arrange.** Framework agreements, supplier lists and stock plans cover AA items (SOPs 6-06, 6-11).\n\n3.  **Declare.** The City Mayor declares a State of Imminent Disaster after the PDRA, CDRRMC recommendation and RDRRMC process (Chapter 1, SOP GOV-05).\n\n4.  **Release.** Budget, Accounting and Treasury release funds immediately, within the tranche rule (SOP 6-05).\n\n5.  **Deliver.** Lead offices carry out AA measures; the No Regrets Principle applies.\n\n6.  **Lift and report.** The declaration lifts on hazard occurrence or on the Mayor''s lifting; unused AA funds accrue to the STF; the 45-day report includes AA fund use (Chapter 7).\n\n**Table 6.41**\n\n*Tranche Worksheet for Hydrometeorological and Geological Hazards*\n\n| **Line** | **Item**                                                      | **Formula**             | **Example (CY 2026 Base)** |\n|----------|---------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------|----------------------------|\n| a        | LDRRMF for the year                                           | From FIN-F01            | PHP 139,955,741.40         |\n| b        | 70% component                                                 | a × 0.70                | PHP 97,969,018.98          |\n| c        | AA line in the LDRRMFIP                                       | not more than b × 0.10  | up to PHP 9,796,901.90     |\n| d        | Cap for interventions more than 3 days before forecast impact | c × 0.30                | PHP 2,939,070.57           |\n| e        | Allowance for interventions within 3 days of forecast impact  | c × 0.70                | PHP 6,857,831.33           |\n| f        | Already disbursed this year from the AA line                  | From FIN-F06            | —                          |\n| g        | Available for this declaration                                | c − f, split by d and e | —                          |\n\n*Note. Illustration only: the CY 2026 plan has no AA line, and the base may change once the Budget Office confirms the regular-revenue computation (A4.1). Sources not subject to graduation: STF balances within their five-year period; partner, private and international donors; ODA; other LGUs; other lawful sources (IRR Rule V Secs. 1(b) and 2). Slow-onset hazards are not graduated until the NDRRMC guidelines issue, but never exceed the year''s AA line (ADR-025 item 4).*\n\n## Annex 6-D. Prepositioned Stock Planning Worksheet\n\nUsed in SOP 6-11 step 1. One worksheet per priority hazard scenario; the highest result per item sets the level. Figures are entered by the CSWDO and the CDRRMO from the approved contingency plans; none is set in this Manual.\n\n**Table 6.42**\n\n*Stock Planning Worksheet*\n\n| **Line** | **Item**                                                     | **Formula or Source**                            | **Entry** |\n|----------|--------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|-----------|\n| a        | Hazard and scenario                                          | Contingency plan (Chapter 3)                     |           |\n| b        | Families to be served, by cluster of barangays               | CP Forms; CDRA exposure                          |           |\n| c        | Days of self-reliance before augmentation                    | CP; DSWD Field Office VIII                       |           |\n| d        | Packs per family per day (food) / kits per family (non-food) | CSWDO standard                                   |           |\n| e        | Target level by item                                         | b × c × d (food); b × d (kits)                   |           |\n| f        | National minimum                                             | DPMS Vol. 2: 500 food packs and 500 hygiene kits | 500 / 500 |\n| g        | Level adopted                                                | Higher of e and f                                |           |\n| h        | Procurement or call-off lead time (days)                     | FIN-F08 agreement                                |           |\n| i        | Average daily issue in an event                              | Past events; AARs                                |           |\n| j        | Reorder point                                                | h × i, plus a safety margin set by the CSWDO     |           |\n| k        | Warehouse split                                              | By cluster and hazard exposure (LOG-F02)         |           |\n| l        | Annual cost of holding and rotation                          | Into the stock replenishment line (SOP 6-01)     |           |\n\n## Validation and Source Control Register\n\n**Table 6.43**\n\n*Validation and Source Control Register*\n\n| **Item**                                                                                                  | **Source Used**                                                             | **Status**                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| CY 2026 LDRRMF figures                                                                                    | CDRRMC Res. No. 05, s. 2025                                                 | Verify SP adoption of the CY 2026 plan                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| LDRRMF base                                                                                               | Res. No. 05, s. 2025 (NTA only)                                             | Budget Office to confirm                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| AA rules                                                                                                  | RA 12287 IRR Rule V, certified true copy read 11–12 Nov 2026                | Medium confidence until the City Legal Office confirms; DBM–COA guidelines pending                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| Emergency procurement ground and documents                                                                | RA 12009 Sec. 35(b); GPPB Circular No. 06-2026                              | Confirm IRR details with the BAC Secretariat                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| Framework agreements                                                                                      | RA 12009 Sec. 16; GPPB Circular No. 07-2026 (23 Jul 2026)                   | Confirm templates with the BAC Secretariat                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| Emergency procurement for anticipatory action: GPPB Res. No. 17-2026 / Circular No. 08-2026 (14 Aug 2026) | Cited in project planning notes; not yet verified as in force               | Cited in project planning notes only. The GPPB announced disaster preparation and response procurement guidelines in 2026, but no copy of Res. 17-2026 was retrieved on 12 Nov 2026. BAC Secretariat to obtain the certified copy and confirm its use in SOPs 6-05 and 6-07 |\n'
